plugin-hostd-protocol (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.21.0, above every version python3-plugin-hostd-protocol had when
    plugin-hostd built it (0.20.6): this source released it at 0.8.1, which
    apt takes only as a downgrade, so a plain upgrade kept 0.20.6 (#180).
  * libplugin-hostd-protocol0 provides plugin-hostd-protocol, the name of the
    library's RPM, which plugin-hostd-full depends on (#180).
  * tools/served-floor.py: the release refuses a version below the highest
    the channel ever served any of this source's packages at, read from the
    history of the channel's ledgers; every pull request runs it (#180).
  * The domain hosting-verb carries its translations (contract.d/hosting-verb/
    catalogs, installed with it): the three HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS words moved
    from omx-clap-core's catalogs word for word (ruling R5), held by
    check-catalogs.
  * plugin-db's package is no longer rendered here (#163):
    plugin_db_vocabulary.h, its render, its check and its install are gone,
    and the build depends on no plugin-db package. The pin words are this
    package's domain pin (#164).
  * One TypeScript encoder (#106): the npm package's ./client writes and
    reads its lines through the codec's Protocol, its command port and reply
    cap the table's constants (message_max, from SOCKET_MSG_MAX_SIZE, is one
    now); the ./lines and ./vocabulary exports, their files and
    tools/ts-client-gen.py are gone.
  * V16 as ruled 2026-11-23: the protocol's words are the domain
    plugin-hostd-protocol, installed as
    contract.d/plugin-hostd-protocol/plugin-hostd-protocol.json, every item
    named PLUGIN_HOSTD_PROTOCOL_* (REPLY_CODES, DAEMON_VERBS, LIBRARY_VERBS,
    EXTENSIONS); it no longer shares <contractdir>/plugin-hostd/ with
    plugin-hostd's package and nested domains. No C macro changes.
  * The TypeScript codec reads the domains in one loop, as the Python codec.
  * The build reads nothing of omx-clap-core (#67): what the two share is
    this package's. The domains host (HOST_REPLY_CODES, HOST_TRACK_KINDS,
    HOST_EVENTS) and hosting-verb (HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS) are installed with
    this contract, and the verbs omx-clap-host shares with plugin-hostd and
    the ones it adds are the items PLUGIN_HOSTD_PROTOCOL_SHARED_VERBS and
    PLUGIN_HOSTD_PROTOCOL_CLAP_HOST_VERBS of the domain
    plugin-hostd-protocol. Their macros are rendered into
    plugin_hostd_protocol_host_verbs.h and
    plugin_hostd_protocol_vocabulary.h; omx_clap_host_verbs.h and
    omx_clap_vocabulary.h are gone, and so is the omx-clap-contract
    dependency.
  * The descriptions store's ask words (#128): add's optional last word
    ask | no-ask, the verb description_get <uri> answered
    <sha256> <lv2|clap> <uri> <base|system|user>, the event
    description_changed <uri>; -529 and -530 also answer description_get.
  * The setting ask_unknown (#157): auto (the default), 1 or 0, a word of
    PHD_CONF_STRINGS with its words in PHD_ASK_UNKNOWN_MODES; the add word
    ask | no-ask overrides it for that add.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:10:00 +0000

